				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

Solid Waste District		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc059ff17c-9356-42df-9a2a-69f7cfaeea0b" data-containerid="059ff17c-9356-42df-9a2a-69f7cfaeea0b" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  >
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="bd663ba4-1a78-45d3-a502-71d9fcda13eb">				
	<div class="row nest first wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id43d4e853-42cf-4f31-9bbf-9f877bf29581" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="43d4e853-42cf-4f31-9bbf-9f877bf29581">	

<div class="widget image pageStyles" id="divImageOuter9bbbf92a-c5c4-4b9b-97d8-a50a85ee8237" data-widget-id="9bbbf92a-c5c4-4b9b-97d8-a50a85ee8237">
    
	<div class="widgetBody imageBorder" id="divImage9bbbf92a-c5c4-4b9b-97d8-a50a85ee8237"><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentID=6378" alt="Clark County Solid Waste District Recycling Center" title="Clark County Solid Waste District Recycling Center"/>	</div></div>

	</div> <!-- inner column -->

	</div> <!-- inner row -->
	<div class="row nest last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id5df2fedd-c381-496c-97d1-70a1c1096cfb" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="5df2fedd-c381-496c-97d1-70a1c1096cfb">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor56875019-3653-4618-9e25-f754032ed936" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1"><strong>2026 Great American Cleanup</strong></h2><p>The Great American Cleanup is a volunteer program under Keep America Beautiful that helps clean and beautify the green spaces of Clark County through the Keep Clark County Beautiful (KCCB) program.</p><p>KCCB would like to say thank you for a successful 2026 Great American Cleanup! There were 800 volunteers from individuals, scouts, schools, and clubs that helped remove 136 bags of litter across the county. The Downtown Cleanup is the KCCB Earth Day cleanup and there were over 60 volunteers that removed 57 bags of litter in the 40+ blocks of the core of Downtown Springfield.&nbsp;</p><p>THANK YOU for your time and effort and watch your emails and our Keep Clark County Beautiful Facebook page for 2027 Great American Cleanup details and registration information in February.</p><h3>Make Clark County a Litter Bit Better Program seeking businesses</h3><p><br>The Clark County Solid Waste District and Keep Clark County Beautiful are seeking businesses to participate in our Make Clark County A Litter Bit Better program, our business community volunteer cleanup initiative.</p><p>The program is designed to allow businesses an opportunity to volunteer in their community. The Solid Waste District will provide the cleanup supplies -- all you need to do is show up.</p><p>To schedule a cleanup, call 937-521-2020.</p><h3 id="isPasted">KCCB Seeks Youth Representative</h3><p>The Keep Clark County Beautiful (KCCB) board is seeking a youth representative. Any Clark County high school student with a GPA of at least 3.0 (on 4-point scale) is eligible. The youth representative will be expected to attend board meetings six times a year, serve on a subcommittee, and volunteer for events as available. The term is now until June 30, 2027.</p><p>KCCB is the local affiliate of Keep America Beautiful, the nation&apos;s largest volunteer-based organization, and focuses on litter prevention, waste reduction, and beautification. Applications for this position are available through high school counselors or by calling Sam Perin at (937) 521-2022. Candidates should send applications to Sam Perin, Keep Clark County Beautiful, 1602 W. Main St., Springfield, OH 45504. If applying electronically, send your email to <a href="mailto:sperin@clarkcountyohio.gov">sperin@clarkcountyohio.gov</a>.&nbsp;</p><h3 class="subhead2 " aria-level="2" role="heading">Cleanup Trailer is ready<br><br></h3><p>The Community Cleanup Trailer is available for groups of at least 5 adult volunteers to use for a neighborhood beautification project from March 15 through Nov. 15.</p><p>Our staff will deliver the trailer to, and pick up from, your site. A group can keep the trailer, which is stocked with landscaping tools, for three days.</p><p>Reservations for the trailer are taken on a first-come, first-serve basis. Call Bonnie at 521-2020.</p><p>Full details are on the Cleanup Trailer Page.</p><h3 class="subhead2 " aria-level="2" role="heading">Visit KCCB on Facebook</h3><p><br>Keep Clark County Beautiful has a page on <a href="http://www.facebook.com/#!/pages/Keep-Clark-County-Beautiful/290887661612">Facebook.</a> The page has tips on ways to reduce your waste and photo galleries of KCCB&rsquo;s projects, including the national award-winning Clark County Sunflower Field. Become a fan and check us out!</p>
    </div>

